  "mechanism_class": "structural",
  "mechanism_rationale": "In rhbi-v7 (readout-c162cb8fb6ab4d55620a8693), masking off-diagonal zero-distance pairs (c_hat_xx <= 1e-12) combined with Pareto-protected Weyl-stratified simplicial manifold projection (rhbi_simplex_weight=0.35) unlocked both held discrete image benchmarks img_blobs4 (hq=0.96875) and img_intensity2 (hq=0.90625) while preserving img_stripes2 (hq=1.0) and all 82/115 counted view requirements, and matched float32 continuous MoG tasks bit-for-bit. However, on quantized 8-bit MXFP8 and 4-bit NVFP4 1D Gaussian benchmarks, distinct continuous MoG draws (z_i != z_k) collide onto identical quantized output stairsteps (Q(G(z_i)) == Q(G(z_k))), so output-only zero-distance masking falsely discarded valid quantized bin multiplicity and regressed precision_gaussian_mxfp8 (std_ratio=1.1052 > 1.10) and precision_gaussian_nvfp4 (cdf_ks=0.0777 > 0.05). Binding off-diagonal zero-distance clone deduplication strictly to zero-noise discrete ParticlePrior codebooks via rhbi_self_coupling='feydy_discrete' preserves exact empirical bin multiplicity on continuous-density priors (restoring bit-for-bit rhbi-v6 trajectories on precision_gaussian_fp32, precision_gaussian_mxfp8, and precision_gaussian_nvfp4) while retaining bit-for-bit rhbi-v7 trajectories across all discrete ParticlePrior tasks including img_blobs4, img_intensity2, and img_stripes2.",
